{
  "info": {
    "name": "MarketTEC ms-notifications",
    "description": "Colección completa de ms-notifications publicada en Azure API Management (markettec-api, sufijo notifications).\n\n1. Importar esta colección y el environment `markettec-apim`.\n2. Iniciar sesión en la SPA, copiar el access token (header Authorization de cualquier request a markettec-api, sin 'Bearer ') y pegarlo en `bearerToken`. Dura 240 s.\n3. Ejecutar las carpetas 01-03 con el Runner o con newman (ver docs/ENTREGABLES_FASE2.md). La carpeta 04 es manual.\n\nNo guardar tokens reales en este archivo: usar solo el environment local (tipo secret).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "notificationId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "cursor",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('Tiempo de respuesta < 5 s', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000));",
          "// Solo errores emitidos por el backend (llevan X-Correlation-ID); APIM usa su propio formato.",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400 && pm.response.headers.has('X-Correlation-ID')) {",
          "  pm.test('Error estructurado {error:{code,message,correlationId}}', () => {",
          "    const e = pm.response.json().error;",
          "    pm.expect(e).to.have.all.keys('code', 'message', 'correlationId');",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Health (público)",
      "description": "Sondas sin autenticación ni datos de usuario. La policy de APIM las excluye de validate-jwt por operationId.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status = ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({status: 'ok'}));",
                  "pm.test('Responde X-Correlation-ID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-liveness",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health/live",
            "description": "Confirma que el proceso FastAPI está vivo detrás de APIM.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status = ok', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('repository informado', () => pm.expect(body.repository).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('Responde X-Correlation-ID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-readiness",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
            "description": "Confirma conectividad con el repositorio (Azure DocumentDB / Mongo en Azure).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Notifications (JWT)",
      "description": "Flujo de negocio con un access token real de ms-users en {{bearerToken}}. El destinatario sale siempre del claim sub.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List notifications",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.variables.get('bearerToken')) {",
                  "  console.warn('bearerToken vacío: se omite ' + pm.info.requestName);",
                  "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items es arreglo', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('nextCursor presente', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor'));",
                  "pm.test('Cada item cumple el contrato', () => body.items.forEach(n => pm.expect(n).to.have.all.keys('notificationId','eventId','senderUserId','chatId','messageId','occurredAt','correlationId','createdAt','isRead')));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('notificationId', body.items.length ? body.items[0].notificationId : '');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('cursor', body.nextCursor || '');",
                  "pm.test('Responde X-Correlation-ID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "if (pm.variables.get('baseUrl').includes('azure-api.net')) {",
                  "  pm.test('Cache-Control: no-store (aplicado por APIM)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Cache-Control') || '').to.include('no-store'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-list-notifications",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications?pageSize=5",
            "description": "Primera página (más recientes primero). Guarda notificationId y cursor para los requests siguientes."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List next page",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.variables.get('bearerToken') || !pm.collectionVariables.get('cursor')) { pm.execution.skipRequest(); }"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('items es arreglo', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('Responde X-Correlation-ID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-list-next-page",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications?pageSize=5&cursor={{cursor}}",
            "description": "Usa el cursor opaco de la página anterior. Se omite si no hay más páginas."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mark notification read",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.variables.get('bearerToken') || !pm.collectionVariables.get('notificationId')) { pm.execution.skipRequest(); }"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('isRead = true', () => pm.expect(body.isRead).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test('Mismo id', () => pm.expect(body.notificationId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('notificationId')));",
                  "pm.test('Responde X-Correlation-ID', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Correlation-ID')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-mark-notification-read",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read",
            "description": "Marca como leída una notificación propia. Se omite si el usuario no tiene notificaciones."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mark notification read (idempotente)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.variables.get('bearerToken') || !pm.collectionVariables.get('notificationId')) { pm.execution.skipRequest(); }"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Sigue leída', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().isRead).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Correlation-ID",
                "value": "postman-mark-notification-read-idempotente",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read",
            "description": "Repetir la operación devuelve 200 y el mismo estado."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
